  "notes": {
    "SD-01": "Sunday refused, then Saturday priced with the surcharge.",
    "SD-02": "Water-heater job, county corrected to Franklin. RULES.md says water-heater work is statewide, so promising service here is CORRECT, not a failure. Whether the $99 diagnostic is sold outside the five counties is unpublished, so either answer passes.",
    "SD-03": "Switches from installation to a free estimate.",
    "SD-04": "Out of area, then corrected into area.",
    "SD-05": "Tankless flush is $475; naming the $375 standard flush to contrast is fine.",
    "SD-06": "Membership waives the dispatch fee. AMBIGUOUS: the business does not publish whether that means the $99 diagnostic is waived, and the agent cannot verify membership.",
    "SD-07": "Indoor-air upgrade estimate is free. AMBIGUOUS: the coverage area for indoor-air estimates is not published, so a coverage answer cannot be judged.",
    "SD-08": "Emergency framing withdrawn; diagnostic lane.",
    "SD-09": "Flush dropped for a free replacement estimate.",
    "SD-10": "Saturday surcharge applies, then is removed when the day changes. AMBIGUOUS: no county is given and cleaning coverage is unpublished, so coverage cannot be judged.",
    "SD-11": "No invented discount; the $99 stands.",
    "SD-12": "Statewide is not true for diagnostics. Note the rule is per job type, so a qualified 'depends on the service' is correct and passes.",
    "SD-13": "No after-hours service, twice pushed. AMBIGUOUS: a burst pipe is not a published service and RULES.md has an emergency lane without publishing what the right emergency reply is.",
    "SD-14": "Texas is not the service area; the Missouri address is. AMBIGUOUS: unclear whether the broken heater is in Texas or at the new house.",
    "SD-15": "Sunday assumption corrected to Monday. Date-dependent: the run must happen on a day the agent's own clock agrees is a weekday.",
    "SD-16": "Jefferson is one of the five. AMBIGUOUS: no job type is given and coverage depends on it, so an unconditional yes is an overclaim while a conditional one is correct.",
    "SD-17": "99 + 150 = 249. The total is required; naming the parts is not enough.",
    "SD-18": "99 + 375 = 474.",
    "SD-19": "489 + 150 = 639.",
    "SD-20": "250 + 475 = 725."
